      "message": "I figured this is actually wrong.\n\nI have some trouble keeping path fd for the child process (which runs in a separate SELinux domain), *after* SELinux is enforced.  Then I realized sharing the directory path as FD doesn\u0027t really mean anything, since the child process could create the same path fd by itself.  I think this is why I\u0027ve had trouble with O_PATH/O_DIRECTORY for several times before.\n\nHaving said that, the code change would be fine to land, as it only changes the fd owner type, and I could rephrase the change description.  But it doesn\u0027t really give us anything.\n\nI\u0027ll abandon this change and really fix the client to not pass a path FD instead.",
